 :body "# ADR-2607051500: kotoba-lang/browser split — org-w3-aria\n\n**Status**: accepted (implemented)\n**Date**: 2026-07-05 (session-numbered; see repos.edn ADR numbering convention)\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n\nSee the companion .md file (90-docs/adr/2607051500-browser-aria-split.md) for full prose: Context, Decision, Consequences, One-line summary.\n\nSummary: split kotoba-lang/browser's pure WAI-ARIA accessibility-tree projection (accessible-node/tree and their helpers, browser/accessibility.cljc lines 1-464, zero kotoba-lang deps) into a new, dependency-free repo kotoba-lang/org-w3-aria (aria.core namespace), following this org's established org-<standards-body>-<spec> naming convention (sibling of org-khronos-glb/org-w3-webgpu). browser's own OS-surface/window-manager-specific accessibility projection (surface-tree/session-tree, lines 466-571) stays in browser, now built on top of aria.core instead of duplicating it. browser's existing accessibility_test.clj (388 lines, pipeline-integration tests through browser.core/load-html) stays unchanged since it exercises the real end-to-end delegating pipeline, not aria.core's internals in isolation; org-w3-aria gets new, independent unit tests built on hand-constructed plain-map documents."}
